# Project Data Pipeline

`data/national-commercial-projects.json` is generated output. Editing it directly
is wasted work, because `scripts/merge-national-corpus.py` overwrites it from the
per-state files.

## Correct order

1. Edit `data/states/*.json`, the source of truth for the 50 states.
2. Run `python3 scripts/merge-national-corpus.py` to rebuild the merged corpus.
3. Run `npm run build`.

Corpus-wide text fixes belong in a script under `scripts/` that walks
`data/states/*.json`, so the fix survives the next capture run. See
`scripts/clean-dashes.py`.

## Dry run text transforms first

Print before and after pairs for a handful of representative inputs before writing
to 50 files. A naive capitalisation pass produced "Eearly" and "Ttotal" across the
whole corpus because the replacement inserted a capital without consuming the
original character. The dry run caught it; a blind run would have shipped it.

## Metadata lives in the merge script

`capture_method` and `notes` in the merged file come from
`scripts/merge-national-corpus.py`, not from the state files. Fix that text there.

## Known gaps

- Some Chicago records are named "Chicago Permit #101082051, 707 W JUNIOR TER"
  because the permit feed has no project title. These need better names.
- Public permits and press almost never name a manufacturer. Expect brand mention
  counts near zero until specification extraction ships, and never present that
  zero as a lost bid.

## State playbooks

Every state has a playbook at **`docs/states/{code}.md`** and a matching Cursor rule at
**`.cursor/rules/state-{code}-commercial-pull.mdc`**.

Before any state pull:

1. Read `docs/states/{code}.md`
2. Follow `.cursor/rules/state-data-pull-review.mdc` when the pull finishes
3. Run `python3 scripts/sync-state-playbooks.py --state {code}` to refresh counts

Georgia is the deepest playbook today. Use it as the template when a state graduates
from web research to automated feeds.
